      "analytePanel": "Srinagar MAGLUMI X6 (unit X6-01, software V1) assay menu captured from Parameter Definition > Assay Parameters on 2026-09-25 (49 assays incl. superseded generations and hidden _Mc/_Nt confirmatory channels). analyzerCode is the on-analyzer LIS Channel No.",
      "source": "Wire protocol from the eLab Assist capture logINMessage 21-24 Sep 2026 (COM6): the X6 speaks the same ASTM dialect as the MAGLUMI X3 — Q|1|^SID||ALL query, results as H/P/O/R/L with no frame numbers or checksums, header sender \"X6 User\", and it accepts the X3-style simple-framed order whose header still says \" MAGLUMI X3 \". Noble targets chosen from an aggregate read of this site's filled result rows over the last 180 days and of the rows behind the captured barcodes.",
      "_protocolNotes": [
        "The X6 matches an ORDERED channel to whichever reagent generation is on board and labels the UPLOAD with that generation's LIS Channel No.: eLab ordered \"CEA\" and got \"CEA II\" back, ordered \"PROG\" and got \"PROG II\", ordered \"tPSA II\" and got \"PSA\". Synapse orders the channel captured from the screen (analyzerCode) and resolves uploads by either instrumentCode or analyzerCode, so either label files.",
        "Superseded generations still in the menu (TSH, T3 [ng/dL], TEST [ng/mL], E2, ANA, CCP, FT3, FT4, Vit B12 II [a=1.5]) are not separate Synapse channels. An upload labelled \"TSH\"/\"E2\"/\"ANA\"/\"FT3\"/\"FT4\" resolves to the same row by instrumentCode and files; \"T3\" (ng/dL) is converted x1/100 to the ng/mL field; \"TEST\", \"CCP\", \"Vit B12 II\" match nothing and are dropped.",
        "Rubella IgM_Mc / TOXO IgM_Mc (index) and HBsAg Quant_Nt are hidden confirmatory channels (\"Do not show in Other Interfaces\") and are not mapped.",
        "Out-of-range uploads carry \"<\" / \">\" in the abnormal-flag field (e.g. 25-OH VD II 150 ng/mL \">\", TT3 II 0.6 ng/ml \"<\"); the value is the measuring-range limit and the flag is dropped on write.",
        "Serial: eLab listened on COM6; the port speed was not in the capture — confirm on the analyzer's LIS setup screen (SNIBE default 9600 8-N-1). Tick Host Query in Synapse so the Q|1|^SID query is answered.",
        "Manually diluted re-runs are queried and uploaded with a suffixed SID (\"9457510 dil\") which is not a registered barcode; they are not filed."
      ],
